00:23:36,980 --> 00:23:42,560
A survey is a study, generally in the form of an interview or a questionnaire that

248
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:46,920
provides information concerning how people think and act.

249
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:52,560
In the United States, the best -known surveys are the Gallup Poll and the Harris

250
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:57,780
Poll. As anyone who watches much as the news during presidential campaigns knows,

251
00:23:58,220 --> 00:24:03,660
these polls have become an important part of political life in the United States.

252
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:08,280
North Americans are familiar with the many person -on -the -street interviews on

253
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:10,060
local television news shows.

254
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:15,420
While such interviews can be highly entertaining, they are not necessarily an

255
00:24:15,420 --> 00:24:17,560
accurate indication of public opinion.

256
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:22,580
First, they reflect the opinions of only those people who appear at a certain

257
00:24:22,580 --> 00:24:28,660
location. Thus, such samples can be biased in favor of commuters, middle -class

258
00:24:28,660 --> 00:24:34,140
shoppers, or factory workers, depending on which area the news people select.

259
00:24:34,860 --> 00:24:40,040
Second, television interviews tend to attract outgoing people who are willing to

260
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:45,260
appear on the air, while they frighten away others who may feel intimidated by a

261
00:24:45,260 --> 00:24:51,420
camera. A survey must be based on a precise representative sampling if it is to

262
00:24:51,420 --> 00:24:54,660
genuinely reflect a broad range of the population.

263
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:57,900
In preparing to conduct a survey,

264
00:24:58,640 --> 00:25:02,860
sociologists must exercise great care in the wording of questions.

265
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:08,260
An effective survey question must be simple and clear enough for people to

266
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:13,980
understand it. It must also be specific enough so that there are no problems in

267
00:25:13,980 --> 00:25:15,500
interpreting the results.

268
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:21,580
Even questions that are less structured must be carefully phrased in order to elicit

269
00:25:21,580 --> 00:25:23,190
the type of information desired.

270
00:25:24,580 --> 00:25:29,860
Surveys can become indispensable sources of information, but only if the sampling is

271
00:25:29,860 --> 00:25:33,140
done properly and the questions are worded accurately.

272
00:25:33,140 --> 00:25:38,620
There are two main forms of surveys, the interview and the questionnaire.

273
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:43,080
Each of these forms of survey research has its advantages.

274
00:25:43,660 --> 00:25:48,700
An interviewer can obtain a high response rate because people find it more difficult

275
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:53,620
to turn down a personal request for an interview than to throw away a written

276
00:25:53,620 --> 00:25:59,780
questionnaire. In addition, an interviewer can go beyond written questions and probe

277
00:25:59,780 --> 00:26:03,160
for a subject's underlying feelings and reasons.

278
00:26:03,780 --> 00:26:08,940
However, questionnaires have the advantage of being cheaper and more consistent.

